  "_note": "Rigify NEW face rig. Companion to the overhauled flat face BVH (66 face bones, all flat-parented to Head, zero-constraint). Masters-only design: face-anchored target masters driven via BASIS, plus HEAD_LOCAL on bones whose target parent chain rides jaw. The HEAD_LOCAL path uses Blender's pb.matrix setter to back-solve the basis through whatever the target parent did (jaw cascade, constraint blends, anything) — so lip.B can be driven to land at source's exact head-local position without double-counting the parent's contribution. v6 enables HEAD_LOCAL on the LowerLip → lip.B pair (the depth-level view_layer.update() in retarget.py's bake loop makes parent matrices current at the moment of back-solve, so this works correctly). PAIR SELECTION: BASIS for face-anchored masters (jaw_master, jaw.L/R, lip.T, lip_end.L/R.001, eye.L/R, lid.*002, brow endpoints, brow.T.*, cheek.B.*001, cheek.T.*001, nose, nose.002, nose.L/R, forehead.*, temple.*) — these have no parent-cascade contamination. HEAD_LOCAL for LowerLip → lip.B because its target parent chain (MCH-lip_arm.B.L → MCH-jaw_master_bottom_out) rides 100% with jaw. DROPPED still: inner lip tweaks (MCH-lip_offset cascade fills them), jaw chain children (chin / chin.001 / chin.L/R / jaw.L/R.001 — parent ORG-jaw_master 100%, could be re-added as HEAD_LOCAL pairs later if user wants chin articulation), tongue chain (same — could re-add as HEAD_LOCAL), brow ridge middles, brow muscle middle, Nose1/3/4 / nostril ends, ear pairs (source has no ear bones).",
